  "answer_text": "Depending on whether you are looking for real-time data, deep-dive analysis, or quick daily updates, the best places to find the latest stock market news can be categorized into a few main areas:\n\n### 1. Mainstream & Real-Time Financial News (Best for Fast Updates)\nThese platforms are the industry standard for breaking news, live market reactions, and daily developments:\n* **CNBC:** Excellent for real-time market tracking, breaking business news, and live updates during trading hours. \n* **Yahoo Finance:** A fantastic, free resource that offers real-time stock quotes, interactive charts, and aggregated financial news from various sources. You can also build custom watchlists here.\n* **MarketWatch:** Focuses heavily on individual stock movements, market trends, and personal finance with easy-to-read articles.\n* **Reuters & Bloomberg:** These are professional-grade wire services. They provide objective, incredibly fast global market coverage and macroeconomic news. \n\n### 2. Deep-Dive Financial Analysis (Best for Long-Term Investors)\nIf you want to understand *why* markets are moving and need in-depth analysis on company valuations and economic policies:\n* **The Wall Street Journal (WSJ):** The gold standard for business journalism and economic analysis (requires a subscription for full access).\n* **Financial Times (FT):** Offers an excellent, highly-regarded global perspective on international markets, central bank policies, and corporate finance.\n* **Morningstar:** Best known for its unbiased, in-depth research on mutual funds, ETFs, and individual stock valuations.\n* **Seeking Alpha:** A crowd-sourced platform where thousands of independent investors and financial analysts publish detailed thesis papers on individual stocks.\n\n### 3. Interactive Charts & Technical Tools (Best for Active Traders)\nIf you prefer looking at charts, price action, and technical indicators:\n* **TradingView:** One of the most popular platforms for real-time charting, technical analysis, and social sharing of trading ideas.\n* **Investing.com:** Provides free, real-time global market indices, futures, commodities, currencies, and technical tools.\n\n### 4. Community & Sentiment (Best for Social Trends)\n* **Stocktwits:** Often described as \"Twitter for traders,\" this social platform lets you see real-time investor sentiment and discussions about specific stock tickers.\n\n**Recommendation:** For a quick, free daily overview, start with **Yahoo Finance** or **CNBC**. If you are looking to research specific stocks to buy, **Seeking Alpha** or **Morningstar** will serve you best.",
